              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "21 Point Black Tile is a Hearts-style domino game using a double-six set: 21 penalty points per deal. Three or four players pass three tiles left; leader nominates suit each trick. Lowest total score wins."
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Hearts-style adaptation for double-six dominoes; 21 penalty points per deal (variant of 11 Point Black Tile family). Western domino trick-taking."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Setup",
          "subtitle": "Table, deck, equipment, and deal",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "3 or 4 (same as 11 Point Black Tile; hand size varies)"
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Double-six domino set (28 tiles)"
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Double-six domino set"
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Tiles dealt; each player passes 3 face-down to the left before play. First player chosen by drawing highest total from boneyard."
            }
          ]
        }
